WEBVTT

1
00:01:36.539 --> 00:01:38.650
Don't you wish you could paint like that?

2
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.984
Oh, I'm sorry?

3
00:01:40.084 --> 00:01:42.904
I said, don't you wish
you could paint like your husband?

4
00:01:43.004 --> 00:01:46.885
Really. You must be so proud of him.

5
00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:51.246
So elegant.

6
00:01:51.346 --> 00:01:53.957
Yes, they're all Vejle, where he grew up.

7
00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:57.752
Now, I don't say my client is the
best landscape artist in Denmark,

8
00:01:57.852 --> 00:02:00.088
but he is in the top one.

9
00:02:00.188 --> 00:02:01.631
Yes. Oh, hello!

10
00:02:01.731 --> 00:02:03.424
It's going very well.

11
00:02:03.524 --> 00:02:07.495
Mmm. Yes. He'll be impossible.

12
00:02:07.611 --> 00:02:09.662
Oh, my.

13
00:02:16.954 --> 00:02:17.981
Oh, thank you.

14
00:02:18.081 --> 00:02:19.148
And Rasmussen!

15
00:02:19.248 --> 00:02:21.985
Oh, come on. Be kind.
At least he agreed to see your work.

16
00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:24.445
- It was only because he was drunk.
- I know.

17
00:02:24.545 --> 00:02:25.530
Yes, you were loving it.

18
00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.782
I was not!

19
00:02:27.882 --> 00:02:31.185
"I don't say my client is
the best landscape artist in Denmark..."

20
00:02:31.285 --> 00:02:34.122
- But...
- "He's in the top one!"

21
00:02:34.222 --> 00:02:36.124
Quiet! People are sleeping.

22
00:02:36.224 --> 00:02:38.055
Sorry.

23
00:02:58.121 --> 00:03:01.042
Do you know what time it is?

24
00:03:01.624 --> 00:03:03.651
Time you came back to bed?

25
00:03:03.751 --> 00:03:05.502
No.

26
00:03:06.087 --> 00:03:08.838
I'm ready to start work.

27
00:03:10.174 --> 00:03:12.345
- Gerda.
- What?

28
00:03:13.761 --> 00:03:15.932
Your face.

29
00:03:17.473 --> 00:03:22.190
- You think I can't resist you?
- Do you want to resist me?

30
00:03:23.438 --> 00:03:24.631
No.

31
00:03:24.731 --> 00:03:28.942
But I'd like you to ask nicely,
so I don't feel such a pushover.

32
00:03:32.405 --> 00:03:34.576
Gerda Wegener.

33
00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.701
My life.

34
00:03:39.787 --> 00:03:41.808
My wife.

35
00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.744
Thorbjorn.

36
00:03:54.844 --> 00:03:56.725
Mr. Wegener.

37
00:04:02.935 --> 00:04:04.686
Tighter.

38
00:04:15.698 --> 00:04:17.699
Perfect.

39
00:04:24.415 --> 00:04:26.366
Yes. More.

40
00:04:32.965 --> 00:04:34.926
Einar Wegener.

41
00:04:35.176 --> 00:04:37.217
Oh, don't worry about him.

42
00:04:37.679 --> 00:04:40.707
He's only ever had eyes for one woman.

43
00:04:40.807 --> 00:04:42.709
My guilty secret's out.

44
00:04:42.809 --> 00:04:47.422
So, when are you two going
to brood me a godchild, huh?

45
00:04:47.522 --> 00:04:48.881
Ulla, you're an atheist.

46
00:04:48.981 --> 00:04:50.592
Have you tried drinking raw eggs?

47
00:04:50.692 --> 00:04:53.469
- No.
- Do it. For my sake.

48
00:04:53.569 --> 00:04:55.763
- We're trying.
- Try harder.

49
00:04:55.863 --> 00:04:57.098
Anyway...

50
00:04:57.698 --> 00:05:01.603
What are you doing in today?
I thought you had finished last week.

51
00:05:01.703 --> 00:05:05.714
I wanted to check on the painting
of the backdrop for the storm scene.

52
00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.901
And give Gerda some space.

53
00:05:08.001 --> 00:05:10.612
Ah. She's got a shy one?

54
00:05:11.879 --> 00:05:13.448
Well, you know I'm next.

55
00:05:13.548 --> 00:05:15.989
Oh... So I heard.

56
00:05:17.135 --> 00:05:18.494
I won't be shy.

57
00:05:18.594 --> 00:05:20.038
I should imagine not.

58
00:05:20.138 --> 00:05:22.879
She'll need all her colors for me.

59
00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.822
Mmm-hmm.

60
00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.701
Mmm!

61
00:05:42.952 --> 00:05:45.043
Head up.

62
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:53.254
I wanted to say
I appreciate our being alone today.

63
00:05:55.631 --> 00:05:57.742
I hope your husband doesn't mind.

64
00:05:57.842 --> 00:05:59.933
Not at all.

65
00:06:00.261 --> 00:06:05.102
I could see his being here
made you uncomfortable.

66
00:06:05.641 --> 00:06:08.352
It wasn't personal.

67
00:06:09.395 --> 00:06:11.339
It's not uncommon.

68
00:06:11.439 --> 00:06:13.190
Ah.

69
00:06:13.608 --> 00:06:16.511
It's hard for a man
to be looked at by a woman.

70
00:06:16.611 --> 00:06:20.473
Women are used to it,
of course, but for a man to, um,

71
00:06:20.573 --> 00:06:24.227
submit to a woman's gaze.

72
00:06:24.327 --> 00:06:26.868
It's unsettling.

73
00:06:30.025 --> 00:06:33.994
Although I believe there's some
pleasure to be had from it...

74
00:06:34.094 --> 00:06:36.569
once you, um...

75
00:06:37.298 --> 00:06:39.549
yield.

76
00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.870
Sit.

77
00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.851
Good girl.

78
00:07:04.492 --> 00:07:06.663
- Morning.
- Morning.

79
00:07:20.842 --> 00:07:22.593
Well?

80
00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.455
Perfect.

81
00:07:31.185 --> 00:07:32.420
Almost.

82
00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.521
Ah.

83
00:07:45.533 --> 00:07:48.444
- Good luck!
- Toodle-oo!

84
00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.460
All portraits.

85
00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:16.151
Is that bad?

86
00:08:17.273 --> 00:08:19.074
Not per se.

87
00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:36.421
This kind of work is not really my...

88
00:08:38.002 --> 00:08:42.633
Gerda, I don't think it would
benefit either of us to show these.

89
00:08:42.799 --> 00:08:45.910
It's not a judgment on your abilities.

90
00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:48.162
I agree with Einar.

91
00:08:48.262 --> 00:08:53.523
You could be a first-class painter
if you found the right subject matter.

92
00:09:05.196 --> 00:09:06.639
How was it?

93
00:09:06.739 --> 00:09:08.490
Fine.

94
00:09:09.325 --> 00:09:12.116
I finally managed
to get the color for the snow.

95
00:09:12.912 --> 00:09:15.043
A bog in Vejle.

96
00:09:15.665 --> 00:09:18.610
I don't know how you can
paint the same thing over and over.

97
00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:20.820
I suppose I just
haven't finished with it yet.

98
00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:21.946
Gerda?

99
00:09:22.046 --> 00:09:25.877
Could you please not speak
to Rasmussen about me again?

100
00:09:27.635 --> 00:09:29.871
My work is my business.

101
00:09:29.971 --> 00:09:32.432
- Stay out of it.
- Gerda.

102
00:10:00.001 --> 00:10:02.153
I have my period.

103
00:10:02.253 --> 00:10:04.054
Sorry.

104
00:10:04.797 --> 00:10:07.033
- Are you?
- Of course I am.

105
00:10:07.133 --> 00:10:09.344
I mean, you know I am.

106
00:10:15.683 --> 00:10:18.644
Could you help me with something?

107
00:10:20.188 --> 00:10:21.464
Anything.

108
00:10:21.564 --> 00:10:24.050
Ulla has an extra rehearsal.
She canceled again.

109
00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.031
Oh.

110
00:10:26.361 --> 00:10:28.763
Would you try on her stockings and shoes?

111
00:10:28.863 --> 00:10:31.808
I'm just so behind, I don't know how
I'll be finished in time for her opening.

112
00:10:31.908 --> 00:10:34.978
Yeah, I'll... I'll do it.

113
00:10:35.078 --> 00:10:37.619
It's fine, I'll do it.

114
00:10:37.955 --> 00:10:39.786
They're there.

115
00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.602
Hvappe, no, not now.

116
00:11:15.702 --> 00:11:17.562
He almost snagged it.

117
00:11:17.662 --> 00:11:19.583
Hvappe.

118
00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.735
Uh...

119
00:11:23.835 --> 00:11:25.676
That's backwards.

120
00:11:35.138 --> 00:11:37.373
I saw those in the window at Fonnesbech's.

121
00:11:37.473 --> 00:11:39.167
Hmm.

122
00:11:39.267 --> 00:11:42.279
- Smart, aren't they?
- I don't think they'll fit.

123
00:11:42.379 --> 00:11:45.340
Well, you do the best you can.

124
00:12:05.877 --> 00:12:08.196
- No, I need the dress.
- No.

125
00:12:08.296 --> 00:12:11.032
- I need to see how the hem falls.
- No, Gerda, I'm not putting it on.

126
00:12:11.132 --> 00:12:13.883
Well, I haven't asked you to.

127
00:12:18.806 --> 00:12:21.057
Just relax.

128
00:12:21.768 --> 00:12:24.019
The sooner I start,

129
00:12:24.729 --> 00:12:27.150
the sooner I finish.

130
00:13:15.113 --> 00:13:16.954
Well, hello, there!

131
00:13:21.452 --> 00:13:24.293
Oh, don't worry, my darling.

132
00:13:28.543 --> 00:13:31.294
We're going to call you

133
00:13:33.297 --> 00:13:35.048
Lili.

134
00:13:56.404 --> 00:13:58.865
Such concentration.

135
00:14:00.658 --> 00:14:02.143
Sometimes I think you're going to slip

136
00:14:02.243 --> 00:14:04.687
through the surface
of the painting and vanish.

137
00:14:04.787 --> 00:14:06.998
Into the bog.

138
00:14:08.541 --> 00:14:11.672
Like your friend's kite
when you were a boy.

139
00:14:12.003 --> 00:14:13.404
- Hans.
- Mmm.

140
00:14:13.504 --> 00:14:15.715
Yes, Hans.

141
00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:21.913
I bet he still sits on that rock,

142
00:14:22.013 --> 00:14:23.122
sobbing his heart out.

143
00:14:23.222 --> 00:14:25.063
Don't.

144
00:14:26.267 --> 00:14:29.295
He's actually an art dealer in Paris.

145
00:14:29.395 --> 00:14:32.298
- Peddling old masters to rich Americans.
- Hmm.

146
00:14:32.398 --> 00:14:34.175
So we don't need to worry about Hans.

147
00:14:34.275 --> 00:14:37.106
No, we don't need to worry about Hans.

148
00:14:38.905 --> 00:14:40.181
I didn't mean to disturb you.

149
00:14:40.281 --> 00:14:42.350
No, it's okay. I'm finished.

150
00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:45.853
And don't worry, I won't
disappear into the bog.

151
00:14:45.953 --> 00:14:48.714
The bog's in me, silly.

152
00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:09.794
What?

153
00:15:09.894 --> 00:15:13.065
Can't a man watch his wife get undressed?

154
00:15:18.319 --> 00:15:20.096
It's new.

155
00:15:20.196 --> 00:15:22.947
That's very observant.

156
00:15:25.868 --> 00:15:28.039
Oh, no, leave it on.

157
00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:44.221
It's pretty.

158
00:15:46.055 --> 00:15:48.342
I might let you borrow it.

159
00:15:50.018 --> 00:15:52.211
I might enjoy that.

160
00:15:52.311 --> 00:15:53.963
Is there something you'd like to tell me?

161
00:15:54.063 --> 00:15:57.217
- Is there something you'd like to know?
- No.

162
00:15:57.317 --> 00:15:59.398
I'm your wife.

163
00:16:00.361 --> 00:16:02.612
I know everything.

164
00:16:11.539 --> 00:16:13.790
Those two, over there.

165
00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.027
Both of them?

166
00:16:16.127 --> 00:16:17.362
And at the same time.

167
00:16:18.546 --> 00:16:22.033
Oh, married people
are so delightfully easy to shock.

168
00:16:22.133 --> 00:16:25.036
We just pretend to be shocked
because it encourages you.

169
00:16:25.136 --> 00:16:26.579
I know.

170
00:16:26.679 --> 00:16:29.707
That is why you're the only married couple
in my party for the Artists' Ball.

171
00:16:29.807 --> 00:16:31.459
No. Out of the question.

172
00:16:31.559 --> 00:16:32.669
She can go without me.

173
00:16:32.769 --> 00:16:36.881
Gerda without an escort?
Why, it would be a scandal!

174
00:16:36.981 --> 00:16:38.383
Gerda loves a scandal.

175
00:16:38.483 --> 00:16:41.103
- Look at the way she dresses.
- Flaunting her ankles.

176
00:16:41.203 --> 00:16:44.973
I don't think anyone is likely to be
corrupted by seeing my ankles.

177
00:16:45.073 --> 00:16:46.975
I was.

178
00:16:47.075 --> 00:16:49.269
It was the first time we met,
I was leaving the Academy

179
00:16:49.369 --> 00:16:52.950
and she was sitting on the steps,
flaunting said ankles.

180
00:16:54.248 --> 00:16:56.776
And she propositioned me.

181
00:16:56.876 --> 00:16:58.194
Is that true?

182
00:16:58.294 --> 00:17:01.505
When I said hello to him,
he actually blushed.

183
00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:05.577
He was so shy, so I asked him out.

184
00:17:05.677 --> 00:17:07.036
And you said yes.

185
00:17:07.136 --> 00:17:09.137
Well, she made me.

186
00:17:09.847 --> 00:17:13.223
- She seemed so sure.
- I was sure.

187
00:17:13.768 --> 00:17:15.003
I still am.

188
00:17:15.103 --> 00:17:17.814
- Please, enough.
- No.

189
00:17:18.064 --> 00:17:21.858
- What was it about him?
- I don't know.

190
00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:26.451
But we went for coffee, and after,

191
00:17:26.948 --> 00:17:28.699
I kissed him.

192
00:17:30.284 --> 00:17:32.145
And it was the strangest thing.

193
00:17:32.245 --> 00:17:34.626
It was like kissing myself.

194
00:17:35.415 --> 00:17:38.109
These two won't be staying much longer.

195
00:17:38.209 --> 00:17:41.446
Unmarried people
are so delightfully easy to shock.

196
00:17:59.522 --> 00:18:01.403
Leave it.

197
00:18:04.861 --> 00:18:08.140
Were you really corrupted by my ankles?

198
00:18:11.993 --> 00:18:14.744
You were shameless.

199
00:18:16.456 --> 00:18:18.577
I still am.

200
00:19:34.909 --> 00:19:37.145
Beautiful,

201
00:19:37.245 --> 00:19:39.456
shameless Gerda.

202
00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:59.271
Wait.

203
00:20:35.011 --> 00:20:37.122
Did I wake you?

204
00:20:38.473 --> 00:20:39.624
Sorry.

205
00:20:39.724 --> 00:20:41.918
I couldn't sleep.

206
00:20:42.018 --> 00:20:43.979
Why?

207
00:20:45.605 --> 00:20:47.799
Wondering about things.

208
00:20:47.899 --> 00:20:50.218
What things?

209
00:20:50.318 --> 00:20:53.899
Wondering if we made a baby last night.

210
00:20:54.572 --> 00:20:56.823
What do you think?

211
00:20:57.533 --> 00:21:00.562
Wondering when you got so pretty.

212
00:21:00.662 --> 00:21:03.147
I was always pretty.

213
00:21:03.247 --> 00:21:06.918
But you just never noticed.

214
00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:51.251
- Hello?
- In here.

215
00:21:52.547 --> 00:21:55.168
These are good, Gerda.

216
00:21:57.260 --> 00:21:59.181
- You think?
- Mmm.

217
00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:02.415
Well, thank you.

218
00:22:02.515 --> 00:22:04.208
I had a coffee with Ulla.

219
00:22:04.308 --> 00:22:06.794
- Hmm.
- She asked me about the Artists' Ball.

220
00:22:06.894 --> 00:22:08.212
I'm not going.

221
00:22:08.312 --> 00:22:10.840
Don't worry.

222
00:22:10.940 --> 00:22:13.111
I told her no.

223
00:22:14.569 --> 00:22:17.180
You should go. You enjoy it.

224
00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:19.015
With you, I enjoy it.

225
00:22:19.115 --> 00:22:20.475
It's good to be seen at those things.

226
00:22:20.575 --> 00:22:22.977
- I do understand that.
- And that's why you hate them.

227
00:22:23.077 --> 00:22:26.147
I feel as though I'm performing myself.

228
00:22:26.247 --> 00:22:28.900
Giving them your Einar Wegener.

229
00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:30.751
Mmm-hmm.

230
00:22:34.756 --> 00:22:37.700
Why not give them something different?

231
00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:40.221
Go as someone else?

232
00:22:41.429 --> 00:22:44.430
Do you have someone in particular in mind?

233
00:22:49.354 --> 00:22:50.421
No.

234
00:22:50.521 --> 00:22:53.232
You'd be very convincing.

235
00:22:57.320 --> 00:22:58.596
That is outrageous.

236
00:22:58.696 --> 00:23:00.473
Oh, you might even enjoy it.

237
00:23:00.573 --> 00:23:02.324
No.

238
00:23:10.458 --> 00:23:14.039
You'll have to shave closer next time.

239
00:23:22.679 --> 00:23:26.060
Mmm? Mmm.

240
00:23:27.809 --> 00:23:29.294
Close your eyes.

241
00:23:29.394 --> 00:23:31.087
This is hard on someone else.

242
00:23:31.187 --> 00:23:32.978
Well, let me try.

243
00:23:42.490 --> 00:23:44.571
What do you think?

244
00:23:44.993 --> 00:23:47.204
Better than I ever manage.

245
00:23:48.371 --> 00:23:50.162
Lili.

246
00:23:50.373 --> 00:23:52.874
I want to sketch you.

247
00:23:53.459 --> 00:23:55.570
Sit.

248
00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:58.323
Come on, Hvap. Come on, you.

249
00:23:58.423 --> 00:24:00.033
Lean to the side.

250
00:24:00.133 --> 00:24:01.884
Knee over.

251
00:24:03.011 --> 00:24:04.913
Head up. Oh.

252
00:24:05.013 --> 00:24:08.144
Look at those hands. Relax.

253
00:24:24.407 --> 00:24:25.600
Don't make her a slut!

254
00:24:25.700 --> 00:24:27.781
It's your fault.

255
00:24:28.411 --> 00:24:30.104
You excite her.

256
00:24:30.204 --> 00:24:32.125
My, Miss Lili.

257
00:24:32.707 --> 00:24:34.108
You are forward.

258
00:24:34.208 --> 00:24:36.459
You have no idea.

259
00:24:45.970 --> 00:24:48.351
Maybe bring out the hand.

260
00:24:55.313 --> 00:24:57.154
Morning.

261
00:25:04.238 --> 00:25:05.348
Morning, Thorbjorn.

262
00:25:05.448 --> 00:25:07.319
Good morning.

263
00:25:18.252 --> 00:25:20.253
Forward.

264
00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:07.551
Hello?

265
00:26:08.678 --> 00:26:10.759
I was wondering where you were.

266
00:26:11.848 --> 00:26:14.059
It's getting late.

267
00:26:14.517 --> 00:26:16.558
We have plenty of time.

268
00:26:16.894 --> 00:26:18.087
I bought you these.

269
00:26:18.187 --> 00:26:19.938
Ah.

270
00:26:23.234 --> 00:26:25.245
Oh, they're perfect.

271
00:26:27.989 --> 00:26:30.280
Are you sure about tonight?

272
00:26:46.841 --> 00:26:48.762
What is it?

273
00:26:49.969 --> 00:26:52.100
Am I pretty enough?

274
00:26:52.555 --> 00:26:54.926
Of course you are.

275
00:26:57.894 --> 00:27:01.065
I'll never be as pretty as you.

276
00:27:01.397 --> 00:27:03.438
You are so beautiful.

277
00:27:18.039 --> 00:27:19.920
My darling!

278
00:27:20.124 --> 00:27:23.795
Ulla, let me introduce...

279
00:27:24.962 --> 00:27:26.883
It's Lili.

280
00:27:27.632 --> 00:27:29.158
That's right.

281
00:27:29.258 --> 00:27:31.369
Einar's cousin from Vejle.

282
00:27:31.469 --> 00:27:33.121
My dear.

283
00:27:33.221 --> 00:27:35.472
You're exquisite!

284
00:27:36.766 --> 00:27:38.293
In, let's go in.

285
00:27:38.393 --> 00:27:40.194
Come on.

286
00:27:41.396 --> 00:27:44.107
You won't leave me, will you?

287
00:27:45.608 --> 00:27:47.819
No, never.

288
00:28:01.082 --> 00:28:03.213
People are looking.

289
00:28:03.793 --> 00:28:06.504
Well, you're a pretty girl.

290
00:28:06.754 --> 00:28:09.345
You'll have to get used to it.

291
00:28:16.097 --> 00:28:18.138
It's fine.

292
00:28:18.433 --> 00:28:20.251
You're just feeling self-conscious.

293
00:28:20.351 --> 00:28:21.794
Gerda?

294
00:28:21.894 --> 00:28:23.655
Oh...

295
00:28:24.772 --> 00:28:26.215
Go and talk to them.

296
00:28:26.315 --> 00:28:27.759
I'll stay with you.

297
00:28:27.859 --> 00:28:31.262
No, go, I'll be fine.
Please go before they come over.

298
00:28:31.362 --> 00:28:33.323
All right.

299
00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:38.201
Who's that?

300
00:29:30.421 --> 00:29:32.922
Are you a reporter?

301
00:29:35.051 --> 00:29:36.892
No.

302
00:29:37.011 --> 00:29:39.142
A poetess?

303
00:29:57.699 --> 00:30:00.530
Do you know the story of this oak tree?

304
00:30:02.036 --> 00:30:03.787
No.

305
00:30:04.622 --> 00:30:08.943
They say that if you eat its acorns,
you can make a wish.

306
00:30:09.043 --> 00:30:12.214
And become anyone you want for a day.

307
00:30:15.174 --> 00:30:17.635
Why would they say that?

308
00:30:20.388 --> 00:30:22.290
Henrik Sandahl.

309
00:30:22.390 --> 00:30:24.459
At your disposal.

310
00:30:24.559 --> 00:30:26.390
Lili.

311
00:30:28.396 --> 00:30:30.767
Are you here with someone, Lili?

312
00:30:31.399 --> 00:30:33.134
Yes, my, uh...

313
00:30:33.234 --> 00:30:35.405
My cousin's wife.

314
00:30:36.821 --> 00:30:38.742
Who's your cousin?

315
00:30:39.615 --> 00:30:42.576
Einar Wegener. Painter.

316
00:30:42.910 --> 00:30:45.791
Yes, he's rather a good one.

317
00:30:46.664 --> 00:30:49.425
He's better than most people think.

318
00:30:49.917 --> 00:30:51.027
Is that right?

319
00:30:51.127 --> 00:30:53.918
Most people our age, at any rate.

320
00:30:59.260 --> 00:31:04.011
Don't go back in there.
It's, um... It's cooler out here.

321
00:31:05.141 --> 00:31:07.168
Besides, I'm a romantic.

322
00:31:07.268 --> 00:31:09.059
Really?

323
00:31:09.354 --> 00:31:11.172
I prefer the shadows.

324
00:31:11.272 --> 00:31:14.384
And I don't mean to presume,

325
00:31:14.484 --> 00:31:17.035
but I've been watching you.

326
00:31:18.613 --> 00:31:20.784
And I think you might be the same.

327
00:31:27.789 --> 00:31:29.620
Come on.

328
00:31:38.800 --> 00:31:40.952
Have you seen Einar? I can't find him.

329
00:31:41.052 --> 00:31:43.663
Of course you can't. He isn't here.

330
00:31:46.974 --> 00:31:48.895
Cheers.

331
00:31:51.688 --> 00:31:53.381
You're different from most girls.

332
00:31:57.694 --> 00:31:59.387
That's not a very original line.

333
00:31:59.487 --> 00:32:01.278
It's true.

334
00:32:03.241 --> 00:32:05.226
You're old-fashioned.

335
00:32:05.326 --> 00:32:07.327
Provincial.

336
00:32:08.997 --> 00:32:10.773
I'm new to the city.

337
00:32:10.873 --> 00:32:13.254
No, it's more than that.

338
00:32:14.669 --> 00:32:18.800
I feel I'd need to ask your permission
before I kissed you.

339
00:32:24.846 --> 00:32:26.967
I should go and find Gerda.

340
00:32:30.351 --> 00:32:33.102
Why don't you tell her I'll walk you home?

341
00:32:34.564 --> 00:32:36.945
No, she wouldn't like that.

342
00:32:37.066 --> 00:32:40.187
- Lili...
- No, Einar...

343
00:32:40.778 --> 00:32:44.449
He might be waiting for us,
and he wouldn't like this.

344
00:32:44.574 --> 00:32:46.625
Wouldn't he?

345
00:32:47.452 --> 00:32:49.293
No.

346
00:32:52.373 --> 00:32:54.294
Lili...

347
00:32:55.960 --> 00:32:58.001
Lili...

348
00:33:02.383 --> 00:33:04.344
Lili...

349
00:33:25.114 --> 00:33:27.433
You didn't ask permission.

350
00:33:27.533 --> 00:33:30.186
I couldn't risk you saying no.

351
00:33:36.417 --> 00:33:38.168
What's the matter?

352
00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:40.671
I'm sorry.

353
00:33:50.139 --> 00:33:51.970
I'm sorry, I don't know what happened.

354
00:34:22.839 --> 00:34:25.090
How are you?

355
00:34:30.471 --> 00:34:33.222
You were late home last night,
so I thought I'd let you sleep.

356
00:34:35.018 --> 00:34:37.059
How was it?

357
00:34:37.854 --> 00:34:40.315
Did Lili have fun?

358
00:34:57.665 --> 00:35:01.786
I think it would be better
if Lili didn't come here again.

359
00:35:04.839 --> 00:35:06.574
Fine.

360
00:35:06.674 --> 00:35:09.244
Exactly what happened
between you and Sandahl last night?

361
00:35:09.344 --> 00:35:12.121
Nothing. It was nothing.

362
00:35:12.221 --> 00:35:14.249
Did he know it was you?

363
00:35:14.349 --> 00:35:16.376
It wasn't as simple as that.

364
00:35:16.476 --> 00:35:20.597
I watched him kiss you, Einar,
so could you please make an effort?

365
00:35:22.774 --> 00:35:27.178
He may have known who I was,
but I wasn't always me.

366
00:35:27.278 --> 00:35:33.279
There was a moment when I was just Lili,
and I think that he could see that.

367
00:35:33.618 --> 00:35:37.039
- Do you see?
- But Lili doesn't exist.

368
00:35:39.916 --> 00:35:42.110
- We made her up.
- I know.

369
00:35:42.210 --> 00:35:45.841
- We were playing a game.
- I know we were.

370
00:35:46.422 --> 00:35:48.473
But then,

371
00:35:50.885 --> 00:35:52.120
something changed.

372
00:35:52.220 --> 00:35:55.811
This is absurd. We... We need to stop.

373
00:35:55.973 --> 00:35:58.684
You need to stop, Einar.

374
00:35:59.560 --> 00:36:01.481
I am going to try.

375
00:36:27.255 --> 00:36:29.176
Another headache?

376
00:36:30.299 --> 00:36:32.300
It's nothing.

377
00:36:35.930 --> 00:36:37.761
Can I get you anything?

378
00:36:38.850 --> 00:36:40.981
I'm fine.

379
00:36:50.737 --> 00:36:52.805
Maybe you should see a doctor.

380
00:36:52.905 --> 00:36:54.656
Gerda...

381
00:36:54.824 --> 00:36:56.625
I'm fine.

382
00:40:11.312 --> 00:40:13.193
I didn't think you'd come.

383
00:40:15.608 --> 00:40:17.569
No.

384
00:40:18.152 --> 00:40:20.153
Nor did I.

385
00:40:35.545 --> 00:40:38.306
I thought you might not come back.

386
00:40:39.340 --> 00:40:41.034
That's absurd.

387
00:40:41.134 --> 00:40:42.885
Is it?

388
00:40:50.018 --> 00:40:52.019
Come here.

389
00:41:18.546 --> 00:41:20.627
The model...

390
00:41:22.842 --> 00:41:25.183
Einar's cousin.

391
00:41:30.475 --> 00:41:33.276
The resemblance is...

392
00:41:39.025 --> 00:41:40.260
Are there others?

393
00:41:40.360 --> 00:41:43.151
A series back at the studio.

394
00:41:45.531 --> 00:41:47.822
These are different.

395
00:41:48.534 --> 00:41:50.228
For these...

396
00:41:50.328 --> 00:41:52.647
I don't know, there may be a market.

397
00:41:52.747 --> 00:41:54.065
You're taking them?

398
00:41:54.165 --> 00:41:56.246
Well, yes.

399
00:42:10.682 --> 00:42:12.473
Come in.

400
00:42:18.398 --> 00:42:20.508
I haven't got long.

401
00:42:20.608 --> 00:42:23.439
Gerda's seeing Rasmussen.

402
00:42:24.779 --> 00:42:27.700
I don't like all these lies.

403
00:42:29.242 --> 00:42:30.518
She's very protective.

404
00:42:30.618 --> 00:42:32.687
Why don't you just tell her about us?

405
00:42:32.787 --> 00:42:35.158
I couldn't do that.

406
00:42:43.423 --> 00:42:45.384
Sorry.

407
00:42:45.800 --> 00:42:48.051
I don't want to upset you.

408
00:42:52.724 --> 00:42:54.985
Come here.

409
00:43:02.066 --> 00:43:04.777
- No.
- Yes.

410
00:43:10.867 --> 00:43:12.618
Einar.

411
00:43:15.330 --> 00:43:16.397
What?

412
00:43:16.497 --> 00:43:19.118
Come on. Shh. It's all right.

413
00:43:21.336 --> 00:43:23.877
I'm sorry, I don't understand.

414
00:43:26.215 --> 00:43:28.409
I... Lili.

415
00:43:28.509 --> 00:43:30.260
Please.

416
00:43:31.304 --> 00:43:33.685
I don't know what you want.

417
00:43:34.515 --> 00:43:37.476
- I want you.
- I don't know what you mean.

418
00:43:38.019 --> 00:43:40.588
- I want you.
- No!

419
00:43:40.688 --> 00:43:43.341
Lili. Lili. Lili, wait!

420
00:44:46.087 --> 00:44:48.015
Are you all right?

421
00:44:50.265 --> 00:44:52.176
No.

422
00:45:00.893 --> 00:45:04.154
I've been seeing Henrik Sandahl.

423
00:45:17.118 --> 00:45:19.409
I'm...

424
00:45:45.605 --> 00:45:47.548
I thought perhaps you knew.

425
00:45:47.648 --> 00:45:49.342
No.

426
00:45:49.442 --> 00:45:51.743
Not this.

427
00:45:53.321 --> 00:45:55.072
So...

428
00:45:56.866 --> 00:45:59.227
Are you in love with Sandahl?

429
00:45:59.327 --> 00:46:01.408
No.

430
00:46:02.330 --> 00:46:05.066
No, I love you.

431
00:46:05.166 --> 00:46:09.195
Gerda, only you. It's Lili, she...

432
00:46:09.295 --> 00:46:10.363
Be honest.

433
00:46:10.463 --> 00:46:14.367
I need you to believe me, Gerda.
You of all people to understand.

434
00:46:14.467 --> 00:46:18.079
All right.
You need to tell me when Henrik and

435
00:46:18.179 --> 00:46:19.914
Lili

436
00:46:20.014 --> 00:46:22.435
are together, they what? They...

437
00:46:22.642 --> 00:46:24.733
They kiss?

438
00:46:26.938 --> 00:46:29.769
- Has it gone beyond that?
- No.

439
00:46:30.942 --> 00:46:33.011
No, Lili has never gone
further than that with a man.

440
00:46:33.111 --> 00:46:34.262
She wouldn't. She's...

441
00:46:34.362 --> 00:46:35.889
There have been other men?

442
00:46:35.989 --> 00:46:41.916
Wait, there... There was another,
yes, but it was a long time ago.

443
00:46:42.787 --> 00:46:45.690
It was that boy, Hans.

444
00:46:45.790 --> 00:46:47.734
In Vejle.

445
00:46:47.834 --> 00:46:51.095
She fell for him, and

446
00:46:51.504 --> 00:46:54.465
he kissed her. Just once.

447
00:46:56.050 --> 00:47:00.051
But then my father came in
and he caught them.

448
00:47:00.555 --> 00:47:03.606
And he smacked Hans down.

449
00:47:03.850 --> 00:47:06.101
He was so angry.

450
00:47:07.186 --> 00:47:09.437
I don't know what to say.

451
00:47:14.235 --> 00:47:16.026
What?

452
00:47:16.904 --> 00:47:19.641
- I'm so...
- Einar?

453
00:47:19.741 --> 00:47:21.742
I'm so sorry.

454
00:47:22.368 --> 00:47:25.939
- I'm so sorry, I'm not feeling well.
- Einar, what is it? Einar, Einar, Einar!

455
00:47:26.039 --> 00:47:29.150
Einar. What's happened? What's happening?

456
00:47:29.250 --> 00:47:32.591
- I'm all right. I'm all right.
- What? Do you have pain?

457
00:47:50.772 --> 00:47:56.010
So, you saw Dr. Andersen
after a bout of severe nosebleeds,

458
00:47:56.110 --> 00:47:59.138
which you have come to believe

459
00:47:59.238 --> 00:48:04.769
coincide with the stomach cramps,
and on a monthly basis.

460
00:48:04.869 --> 00:48:06.620
Hmm.

461
00:48:07.121 --> 00:48:08.690
So.

462
00:48:08.790 --> 00:48:10.711
How long have you been married?

463
00:48:10.833 --> 00:48:11.859
Six years.

464
00:48:11.959 --> 00:48:13.111
Children?

465
00:48:13.211 --> 00:48:14.862
No.

466
00:48:14.962 --> 00:48:17.343
Is there regular copulation?

467
00:48:18.591 --> 00:48:20.342
Yes.

468
00:48:22.470 --> 00:48:24.330
Perhaps less now than before...

469
00:48:24.430 --> 00:48:26.891
Than before you started
to dress as a woman?

470
00:48:27.433 --> 00:48:30.378
I'm a specialist, Mr. Wegener.
You may be embarrassed.

471
00:48:30.478 --> 00:48:32.213
I am not.

472
00:48:32.313 --> 00:48:35.774
Tell me about Lili.

473
00:48:35.942 --> 00:48:37.719
Where does she come from?

474
00:48:37.819 --> 00:48:39.900
Inside me.

475
00:48:42.740 --> 00:48:49.041
You know, the most likely explanation
for all of this is a chemical imbalance.

476
00:48:49.163 --> 00:48:51.084
- Really?
- Mmm.

477
00:48:51.290 --> 00:48:53.081
Onto the bed.

478
00:48:53.584 --> 00:48:55.653
That would explain the pain,

479
00:48:55.753 --> 00:48:59.741
the confused state of masculinity
and the infertility.

480
00:48:59.841 --> 00:49:03.052
Let's hope it is that,
because that, at least, we can cure.

481
00:49:07.015 --> 00:49:08.583
I don't need to do this.

482
00:49:08.683 --> 00:49:10.043
There's nothing wrong with me.

483
00:49:10.143 --> 00:49:12.211
- That's not true.
- Gerda, this can't be right.

484
00:49:12.311 --> 00:49:14.923
Radiation is a miracle, Mr. Wegener.

485
00:49:15.023 --> 00:49:18.784
It destroys the bad and saves the good.

486
00:49:19.027 --> 00:49:21.358
I'm sure it'll be over quickly.

487
00:49:32.790 --> 00:49:35.381
Lie still, Mr. Wegener.

488
00:50:03.696 --> 00:50:05.657
Mr. Wegener?

489
00:50:05.907 --> 00:50:08.488
How are you feeling this morning?

490
00:50:10.328 --> 00:50:13.329
You hurt Lili.

491
00:50:16.292 --> 00:50:19.673
I'm afraid your husband's
aberrant thinking persists.

492
00:50:21.422 --> 00:50:23.658
Do you keep a lock on your wardrobe?

493
00:50:23.758 --> 00:50:24.742
Of course not.

494
00:50:24.842 --> 00:50:28.263
Mrs. Wegener,
you're not encouraging this delusion?

495
00:50:29.097 --> 00:50:30.999
You do understand that
your husband is insane?

496
00:50:31.099 --> 00:50:34.350
No. That's not true.

497
00:50:34.602 --> 00:50:38.363
We trusted you. We came to you for help.

498
00:51:02.463 --> 00:51:04.714
Gerda!

499
00:51:04.966 --> 00:51:06.618
Where have you been?

500
00:51:06.718 --> 00:51:08.536
Away.

501
00:51:08.636 --> 00:51:10.788
Why? What's wrong?

502
00:51:10.888 --> 00:51:13.041
I sold the Lili portraits.

503
00:51:13.141 --> 00:51:16.878
I have enough interest, now,
to mount a full show.

504
00:51:16.978 --> 00:51:20.729
- That's wonderful.
- And there's more.

505
00:51:23.318 --> 00:51:29.529
The Gallery Etienne Dufour in Paris
wants to represent you.

506
00:51:30.158 --> 00:51:33.199
- In Paris?
- Yes, you must go.

507
00:51:35.830 --> 00:51:38.041
I can't travel just now.

508
00:51:38.333 --> 00:51:41.069
Gerda, this is your moment.

509
00:51:41.169 --> 00:51:43.029
You've waited long enough.

510
00:51:43.129 --> 00:51:45.260
These art dealers can be fickle.

511
00:51:50.386 --> 00:51:52.137
Oh!

512
00:52:16.537 --> 00:52:18.106
What are you doing?

513
00:52:18.206 --> 00:52:20.275
I've been asked to exhibit in Paris.

514
00:52:20.375 --> 00:52:23.111
- That's wonderful.
- Yes.

515
00:52:23.211 --> 00:52:26.948
We have to go. Rasmussen said
it would make all the difference.

516
00:52:27.048 --> 00:52:29.993
Gerda, I'm not sure that I can.

517
00:52:30.093 --> 00:52:31.286
I'll take care of you.

518
00:52:31.386 --> 00:52:35.297
- Yes, but surely there's no rush.
- Can't you just do this one thing for me?

519
00:52:37.100 --> 00:52:39.481
What's happening?

520
00:52:40.728 --> 00:52:42.769
I had a letter from Hexler.

521
00:52:43.481 --> 00:52:45.652
He wants to lock me up.

522
00:52:47.652 --> 00:52:50.823
Everything will work out for us.

523
00:52:51.364 --> 00:52:54.125
Really. I know it.

524
00:52:56.411 --> 00:52:59.162
You just have to trust me.

525
00:53:00.790 --> 00:53:02.831
I do.

526
00:53:25.898 --> 00:53:27.675
Einar's a painter, too.

527
00:53:27.775 --> 00:53:31.012
Oh. Do you exhibit in Paris?

528
00:53:31.112 --> 00:53:34.933
I think my work's a little introspective
for French taste.

529
00:53:35.033 --> 00:53:38.478
Excuse me. Is the model here?

530
00:53:38.578 --> 00:53:40.313
No.

531
00:53:40.413 --> 00:53:44.826
- She stayed behind in Denmark.
- Oh, I was so hoping to meet her.

532
00:53:47.236 --> 00:53:49.387
Madame Gerda Wegener...

533
00:54:07.990 --> 00:54:10.071
No, no.

534
00:54:13.321 --> 00:54:15.702
I'm sorry.

535
00:54:32.840 --> 00:54:34.761
Will you sit for me?

536
00:54:37.053 --> 00:54:38.804
Just as you are.

537
00:54:39.681 --> 00:54:42.432
We haven't done that since art school.

538
00:54:43.685 --> 00:54:48.339
The teacher,
suddenly at the mercy of the student.

539
00:54:48.439 --> 00:54:50.770
You found it exciting.

540
00:54:52.026 --> 00:54:54.437
I can't just now.

541
00:54:55.363 --> 00:54:57.534
I'm sorry.

542
00:54:58.199 --> 00:55:00.450
I miss you.

543
00:55:01.494 --> 00:55:03.755
I miss you working beside me.

544
00:55:05.665 --> 00:55:08.796
I can't remember the landscape anymore.

545
00:55:10.336 --> 00:55:13.667
I can't remember Vejle.

546
00:55:15.842 --> 00:55:18.893
Well, you can help me
with this background.

547
00:55:19.679 --> 00:55:23.640
What does it need? A kettle-hole lake?

548
00:55:24.017 --> 00:55:26.377
A farmhouse? Far off?

549
00:55:26.477 --> 00:55:28.648
Gerda.

550
00:56:09.395 --> 00:56:11.297
Merci.

551
00:58:06.721 --> 00:58:10.583
Well, he's playing with us.
He knows the price.

552
00:58:10.683 --> 00:58:14.128
Look, I have to go,
I have some Danish girl waiting to see me.

553
00:58:14.228 --> 00:58:15.171
All right.

554
00:58:15.271 --> 00:58:17.022
Madame.

555
00:58:24.906 --> 00:58:26.867
Hans Axgil.

556
00:58:27.450 --> 00:58:29.727
Hello. Thank you for seeing me.

557
00:58:29.827 --> 00:58:33.648
Don't thank me yet, I can't represent you.
I don't handle any contemporary art.

558
00:58:33.748 --> 00:58:35.942
Of course. I know that.

559
00:58:36.042 --> 00:58:38.861
The reviews for your show
were terrific, but...

560
00:58:38.961 --> 00:58:43.032
Perhaps if you would let me speak,
things would be clearer.

561
00:58:43.132 --> 00:58:45.201
So, when did you arrive?

562
00:58:45.301 --> 00:58:47.802
Six months, almost.

563
00:58:48.638 --> 00:58:52.934
I don't know why Rasmussen
gave you my number, but I'm happy he did.

564
00:58:53.267 --> 00:58:55.044
I asked him.

565
00:58:55.144 --> 00:58:58.548
I wanted to meet you
to put a face to a name.

566
00:58:58.648 --> 00:59:00.049
Hmm.

567
00:59:00.149 --> 00:59:03.400
I believe you were
a childhood friend of my husband.

568
00:59:04.737 --> 00:59:06.908
You have a husband?

569
00:59:10.410 --> 00:59:12.687
I'm married to Einar Wegener.

570
00:59:12.787 --> 00:59:13.855
Einar?

571
00:59:13.955 --> 00:59:15.106
You remember him?

572
00:59:15.206 --> 00:59:19.457
Of course I remember him.
We were such friends. How is he?

573
00:59:19.794 --> 00:59:21.362
He told me that you kissed him once.

574
00:59:21.462 --> 00:59:23.593
I what?

575
00:59:26.551 --> 00:59:30.204
You're right. You're right, I remember.

576
00:59:30.304 --> 00:59:34.042
We were fooling in the kitchen, and he
was wearing his grandmother's apron.

577
00:59:34.142 --> 00:59:37.211
You know, little boys, playing around.

578
00:59:37.311 --> 00:59:40.048
He just looked so pretty in it.
I had to kiss him!

579
00:59:40.148 --> 00:59:43.439
So, yes, I kissed Einar.

580
00:59:43.901 --> 00:59:46.572
The next thing I know,
his father's chasing me out.

581
00:59:49.532 --> 00:59:51.392
Einar, my God.

582
00:59:51.492 --> 00:59:53.561
Why didn't he come today?

583
00:59:53.661 --> 00:59:55.480
He doesn't know I'm here.

584
00:59:55.580 --> 00:59:58.621
I don't think he'd like me
asking for help.

585
01:00:00.168 --> 01:00:04.299
We don't really know people here.
And Einar is... He's...

586
01:00:04.630 --> 01:00:06.324
He's lost his way.

587
01:00:06.424 --> 01:00:08.034
He's not working.

588
01:00:08.134 --> 01:00:12.225
He needs someone to represent him,
someone who knows him.

589
01:00:14.724 --> 01:00:16.985
He needs a friend.

590
01:00:29.489 --> 01:00:32.308
I have a new dealer coming over later.

591
01:00:32.408 --> 01:00:34.619
I'd like you to meet him.

592
01:00:35.536 --> 01:00:37.814
I don't want a new dealer.

593
01:00:37.914 --> 01:00:40.775
It doesn't make sense to me.
I'm hardly working.

594
01:00:40.875 --> 01:00:43.206
That might change.

595
01:00:43.419 --> 01:00:44.946
I don't think so.

596
01:00:45.046 --> 01:00:46.906
I'm happy helping you.

597
01:00:48.049 --> 01:00:50.180
It's Hans Axgil.

598
01:00:51.386 --> 01:00:55.807
Dinner at La Dauphine at 8:00,
then back here to see the paintings.

599
01:00:56.057 --> 01:00:59.478
He remembers you with great fondness.

600
01:01:11.489 --> 01:01:13.391
It was handmade,
and I've had it since I was four.

601
01:01:13.491 --> 01:01:16.895
You know, Einar's still stricken
with guilt about crashing your kite.

602
01:01:16.995 --> 01:01:19.647
My kite? I'll tease him about that.

603
01:01:19.747 --> 01:01:22.525
No, it's too cruel.

604
01:01:22.625 --> 01:01:25.361
Well, if he ever gets here.
Perhaps he doesn't want to see me.

605
01:01:25.461 --> 01:01:29.302
No. No, it's not that.

606
01:01:31.509 --> 01:01:33.890
Maybe we should order without him.

607
01:01:34.470 --> 01:01:36.351
Does he abandon you often?

608
01:01:37.473 --> 01:01:39.684
Of course not.

609
01:01:40.101 --> 01:01:41.852
I was joking.

610
01:01:48.318 --> 01:01:52.029
I can come back another time,
if you think Einar would prefer it.

611
01:01:52.613 --> 01:01:53.765
Really.

612
01:01:53.865 --> 01:01:55.850
He's expecting you.

613
01:01:55.950 --> 01:01:58.701
And it'll do him good.

614
01:02:02.665 --> 01:02:04.866
I know this.

615
01:02:05.460 --> 01:02:08.071
The fjord at Vejle,
not far from our houses.

616
01:02:08.171 --> 01:02:11.302
Yes, he painted it just before we left.

617
01:02:13.009 --> 01:02:14.760
Lili.

618
01:02:16.554 --> 01:02:18.395
Hans.

619
01:02:18.973 --> 01:02:20.917
May I introduce

620
01:02:21.017 --> 01:02:23.211
Lili Wegener.

621
01:02:23.311 --> 01:02:25.902
Einar's cousin from home.

622
01:02:28.483 --> 01:02:31.744
You cannot imagine how happy I am.

623
01:02:33.571 --> 01:02:39.702
We actually met once before, in Vejle,
but you probably don't remember.

624
01:02:42.830 --> 01:02:44.524
May I take your coat?

625
01:02:44.624 --> 01:02:46.375
Of course.

626
01:02:48.127 --> 01:02:50.458
A digestif, Hans?

627
01:02:54.509 --> 01:02:57.260
It's so chilly all of a sudden.

628
01:02:57.804 --> 01:02:59.914
I feel the cold these days.
I don't know why.

629
01:03:00.014 --> 01:03:01.975
Here.

630
01:03:02.183 --> 01:03:04.144
Thank you.

631
01:03:07.772 --> 01:03:10.633
I'm so sorry that Einar couldn't be here.

632
01:03:10.733 --> 01:03:15.824
He told me how, back in Vejle,
you were his great friend.

633
01:03:16.239 --> 01:03:18.850
- Both always plotting to get away.
- That's true.

634
01:03:18.950 --> 01:03:21.667
Such a tedious place!

635
01:03:23.413 --> 01:03:27.775
He said that you would sit
and you'd look out together,

636
01:03:27.875 --> 01:03:30.786
beyond the fjord, to the sea.

637
01:03:31.212 --> 01:03:32.947
To the future.

638
01:03:33.047 --> 01:03:35.378
We had big dreams, yes.

639
01:03:35.967 --> 01:03:37.878
Yes.

640
01:03:39.053 --> 01:03:42.974
And that you were the only one
that would let him paint in peace.

641
01:03:43.099 --> 01:03:45.460
Who told him it was all right
to be a painter.

642
01:03:45.560 --> 01:03:47.891
He used to sketch my portrait.

643
01:03:48.062 --> 01:03:51.174
Take a stone and draw me on the rocks
at the side of the road.

644
01:03:54.235 --> 01:03:57.824
- I didn't know that.
- Yes.

645
01:04:00.074 --> 01:04:01.643
Would you like to see
more of Einar's work?

646
01:04:01.743 --> 01:04:03.478
- Yes.
- But do we have any?

647
01:04:03.578 --> 01:04:04.979
Of course, Lili.

648
01:04:05.079 --> 01:04:06.856
Could we not do it another time?
Because I just...

649
01:04:06.956 --> 01:04:08.816
I want to hear more about you, Hans.

650
01:04:08.916 --> 01:04:09.984
Are you married?

651
01:04:10.084 --> 01:04:12.635
- Uh, no.
- Well, why not?

652
01:04:15.048 --> 01:04:16.699
You don't mind, do you?

653
01:04:16.799 --> 01:04:20.720
I've been on my own a long time now.
I'm too set in my ways.

654
01:04:22.847 --> 01:04:26.834
I think that marriage is the single thing
we should all hope for in life.

655
01:04:26.934 --> 01:04:28.695
Really?

656
01:04:29.103 --> 01:04:32.234
It creates someone else.

657
01:04:32.690 --> 01:04:35.611
More than just the two of you.

658
01:04:37.612 --> 01:04:40.453
Yes, I think it'd be terrible not to...

659
01:04:42.617 --> 01:04:46.604
I think it'd be terrible... I'm so...
Will you excuse me?

660
01:04:46.704 --> 01:04:48.465
Lili.

661
01:05:02.053 --> 01:05:04.038
You ought to go.

662
01:05:04.138 --> 01:05:05.969
Let me help.

663
01:05:08.184 --> 01:05:10.315
Please.

664
01:05:15.233 --> 01:05:17.404
I'm sorry.

665
01:05:20.989 --> 01:05:23.070
Good night, Lili.

666
01:05:23.741 --> 01:05:25.832
Good night.

667
01:05:34.544 --> 01:05:37.505
I don't think he noticed, do you?

668
01:05:38.506 --> 01:05:40.587
I don't know.

669
01:05:41.384 --> 01:05:44.265
I think I got out just in time.

670
01:05:46.097 --> 01:05:48.098
Sleep now.

671
01:05:48.433 --> 01:05:50.684
We'll talk more tomorrow.

672
01:05:52.061 --> 01:05:55.022
Can I borrow a nightdress?

673
01:06:00.403 --> 01:06:02.864
No, we've never done that.

674
01:06:04.365 --> 01:06:07.196
Lili's never spent the night.

675
01:06:08.077 --> 01:06:10.828
It doesn't matter what I wear.

676
01:06:14.459 --> 01:06:16.840
'Cause when I dream,

677
01:06:17.962 --> 01:06:20.713
they're Lili's dreams.

678
01:06:51.621 --> 01:06:53.332
What?

679
01:06:59.921 --> 01:07:01.072
A new dress.

680
01:07:01.172 --> 01:07:03.343
And this is for you.

681
01:07:04.217 --> 01:07:05.910
Do you like it?

682
01:07:06.010 --> 01:07:07.931
Yes.

683
01:07:11.349 --> 01:07:13.167
It's perfect for you.

684
01:07:13.267 --> 01:07:15.003
We're a little short of money
at the moment.

685
01:07:15.103 --> 01:07:16.379
I know.

686
01:07:16.479 --> 01:07:19.060
But now that I'm back,
I can sit for you again.

687
01:07:20.191 --> 01:07:24.282
Well, it worked well before.
Didn't it work?

688
01:07:26.406 --> 01:07:29.817
Come on. Come on, Hvap.

689
01:07:35.164 --> 01:07:36.733
Looks good.

690
01:07:36.833 --> 01:07:38.192
Head up.

691
01:07:38.292 --> 01:07:39.736
Up. There.

692
01:07:39.836 --> 01:07:41.917
- No, back.
- Yes. Okay.

693
01:07:49.637 --> 01:07:52.388
- Is that good?
- Ring, up.

694
01:07:57.854 --> 01:08:00.065
Thank you.

695
01:08:22.337 --> 01:08:24.656
I didn't know you were coming.

696
01:08:24.756 --> 01:08:26.074
It's a good crowd.

697
01:08:26.174 --> 01:08:28.435
She's a popular girl.

698
01:08:29.385 --> 01:08:31.756
Thank you for coming.

699
01:08:32.263 --> 01:08:35.458
Thank you for inviting me.
I thought you'd forgotten all about me.

700
01:08:35.558 --> 01:08:37.639
We've been busy.

701
01:08:38.603 --> 01:08:40.604
Is Einar here?

702
01:08:41.898 --> 01:08:43.174
He hates this kind of thing.

703
01:08:43.274 --> 01:08:44.926
That's a shame.

704
01:08:45.026 --> 01:08:47.187
For you, I mean.

705
01:08:47.528 --> 01:08:48.596
I don't mind.

706
01:08:48.696 --> 01:08:50.598
Is he well?

707
01:08:50.698 --> 01:08:52.529
He's excited.

708
01:08:52.742 --> 01:08:54.435
Our friend, uh, is coming to town,

709
01:08:54.535 --> 01:08:56.312
Ulla Fonsmarck, the dancer.
You maybe know her?

710
01:08:56.412 --> 01:08:59.253
No, I don't think so.

711
01:09:01.292 --> 01:09:03.633
Can I take you to dinner?

712
01:09:04.087 --> 01:09:05.363
To celebrate?

713
01:09:05.463 --> 01:09:07.964
I think someone ought to.

714
01:09:08.383 --> 01:09:10.785
No. Thank you.

715
01:09:10.885 --> 01:09:12.636
Gerda.

716
01:09:13.721 --> 01:09:16.142
Have I offended you?

717
01:09:17.517 --> 01:09:18.960
No.

718
01:09:19.060 --> 01:09:20.811
Gerda.

719
01:09:22.188 --> 01:09:24.399
I'm still Einar's wife.

720
01:09:30.780 --> 01:09:32.531
Hans!

721
01:09:32.991 --> 01:09:34.601
Oh, Henri!

722
01:09:51.467 --> 01:09:53.828
At least take an umbrella.

723
01:09:53.928 --> 01:09:56.372
Oh. No, I'm fine, honestly.

724
01:09:56.472 --> 01:09:58.875
Well, if you just wait a minute,
someone will drive you.

725
01:09:58.975 --> 01:10:01.276
No, I'm fine.

726
01:10:23.499 --> 01:10:25.790
My goodness, you're soaked.

727
01:10:27.712 --> 01:10:29.713
Did it go well?

728
01:10:29.964 --> 01:10:31.805
Tell me, how was it?

729
01:10:33.051 --> 01:10:35.762
You'd know if you'd been there.

730
01:10:37.638 --> 01:10:39.207
I've made us a supper.

731
01:10:39.307 --> 01:10:40.750
You should have come.

732
01:10:40.850 --> 01:10:42.961
A little sort of celebration.

733
01:10:43.061 --> 01:10:45.772
This is not how it goes.

734
01:10:48.149 --> 01:10:50.780
We do these things together.

735
01:10:51.778 --> 01:10:53.930
That was you and Einar.

736
01:10:54.030 --> 01:10:56.766
Stop playing that stupid, stupid game.

737
01:10:56.866 --> 01:10:59.157
Please, Gerda.

738
01:11:00.328 --> 01:11:03.079
Don't you think this is a game.

739
01:11:03.498 --> 01:11:06.067
You should have been there!

740
01:11:06.167 --> 01:11:08.418
How could I?

741
01:11:10.046 --> 01:11:13.797
- Look at me.
- Not everything is about you.

742
01:11:22.517 --> 01:11:24.085
I need to see Einar.

743
01:11:24.185 --> 01:11:25.878
Let me help, please.

744
01:11:25.978 --> 01:11:28.149
I need my husband.

745
01:11:28.898 --> 01:11:31.109
Go get him.

746
01:11:33.528 --> 01:11:35.096
I can't.

747
01:11:35.196 --> 01:11:39.737
I need to talk to my husband.
I need to hold my husband.

748
01:11:41.077 --> 01:11:43.198
I need him.

749
01:11:43.538 --> 01:11:46.289
Can't you just get him?

750
01:11:49.627 --> 01:11:52.168
Can you at least try?

751
01:11:56.634 --> 01:11:58.645
No. I'm sorry.

752
01:12:31.085 --> 01:12:32.836
Gerda.

753
01:12:33.963 --> 01:12:35.714
What is it?

754
01:12:47.143 --> 01:12:49.564
Are you all right?

755
01:13:08.623 --> 01:13:10.624
Oh, my God.

756
01:13:14.295 --> 01:13:15.905
Gerda, wait.

757
01:13:16.005 --> 01:13:17.956
Wait!

758
01:13:49.288 --> 01:13:51.649
I don't think I can

759
01:13:51.749 --> 01:13:54.080
give you what you want.

760
01:14:08.558 --> 01:14:12.019
I don't know how long
we can go on like this.

761
01:14:16.399 --> 01:14:18.360
No.

762
01:14:28.119 --> 01:14:30.063
He needs to see someone.

763
01:14:30.163 --> 01:14:31.940
You know what happened with Hexler.

764
01:14:32.040 --> 01:14:33.921
But he's so thin.

765
01:14:35.001 --> 01:14:37.252
Something's wrong with him.

766
01:14:38.904 --> 01:14:41.085
Lili watches her figure.

767
01:14:41.382 --> 01:14:42.992
Look.

768
01:14:43.092 --> 01:14:47.038
There's a doctor.
He runs the Women's Clinic in Dresden.

769
01:14:47.138 --> 01:14:49.929
He's interested in men like Einar

770
01:14:50.475 --> 01:14:52.085
who are

771
01:14:52.185 --> 01:14:53.946
confused.

772
01:14:55.146 --> 01:14:57.607
Men who are different.

773
01:14:58.441 --> 01:15:00.093
He's often in Paris.

774
01:15:00.193 --> 01:15:02.364
Just talk to him.

775
01:15:09.786 --> 01:15:11.771
You're awake.

776
01:15:11.871 --> 01:15:13.792
How do you feel?

777
01:15:15.625 --> 01:15:17.151
Come.

778
01:15:17.251 --> 01:15:18.945
Listen, I've got somewhere to go.

779
01:15:19.045 --> 01:15:20.806
Where?

780
01:15:23.591 --> 01:15:25.512
Sorry, I...

781
01:15:27.345 --> 01:15:30.186
I don't know
how to hold on to you any longer.

782
01:15:33.643 --> 01:15:35.644
I know.

783
01:15:36.771 --> 01:15:39.152
But I love you,

784
01:15:39.774 --> 01:15:42.535
and I'm going to find an answer.

785
01:16:32.702 --> 01:16:34.395
- English?
- English.

786
01:16:34.495 --> 01:16:36.231
Do you speak English?

787
01:16:36.331 --> 01:16:38.566
Are you, um, a boy or a girl?

788
01:16:38.666 --> 01:16:41.337
- A woman?
- Do you have a...

789
01:16:41.502 --> 01:16:43.170
Or...

790
01:16:47.258 --> 01:16:49.009
Joking.

791
01:17:32.887 --> 01:17:35.678
I can't hold the buyers much longer,
I'm sorry.

792
01:17:42.271 --> 01:17:44.152
Einar?

793
01:17:45.441 --> 01:17:47.652
You're good at this.

794
01:17:48.069 --> 01:17:50.280
I boxed for a while.

795
01:17:51.447 --> 01:17:54.028
Shame you weren't with me earlier.

796
01:18:00.623 --> 01:18:02.650
I'm sorry I've not been to see you before.

797
01:18:02.750 --> 01:18:04.671
That's all right.

798
01:18:05.211 --> 01:18:07.462
You're here now.

799
01:18:08.256 --> 01:18:11.167
I couldn't let Gerda see me like this.

800
01:18:11.592 --> 01:18:13.494
She's had enough to put up with.

801
01:18:13.594 --> 01:18:15.855
What's happened to you?

802
01:18:17.765 --> 01:18:19.846
I don't understand.

803
01:18:21.477 --> 01:18:23.398
Nor do I.

804
01:18:26.482 --> 01:18:29.323
But I don't think it's anything new.

805
01:18:30.445 --> 01:18:32.680
Even back in Vejle...

806
01:18:32.780 --> 01:18:35.031
- What?
- Ow. Sorry.

807
01:18:39.287 --> 01:18:41.198
What?

808
01:18:41.873 --> 01:18:44.124
I was different.

809
01:18:45.460 --> 01:18:48.196
It didn't take much
to be different in Vejle.

810
01:18:48.296 --> 01:18:51.087
Surely that's why we became friends.

811
01:18:53.676 --> 01:18:55.677
Every morning

812
01:18:56.012 --> 01:19:00.853
I promise myself that I will spend
the entire day as Einar.

813
01:19:01.809 --> 01:19:04.671
But there's so little of Einar left.

814
01:19:04.771 --> 01:19:07.692
You think these things
because you're exhausted.

815
01:19:10.985 --> 01:19:14.736
Sometimes I think about killing Einar.

816
01:19:15.573 --> 01:19:20.914
But it's only the thought
that I'd be killing Lili too that stops me.

817
01:19:21.537 --> 01:19:23.748
You need to see someone.

818
01:19:23.998 --> 01:19:25.942
- A doctor.
- No.

819
01:19:26.042 --> 01:19:27.569
- Yes.
- No doctors.

820
01:19:27.669 --> 01:19:30.000
I'll help you find someone.

821
01:19:30.672 --> 01:19:33.213
You have to try.

822
01:19:35.093 --> 01:19:38.288
A confused state of identity.

823
01:19:38.388 --> 01:19:42.584
I drill small holes,

824
01:19:42.684 --> 01:19:45.445
here and here.

825
01:19:45.645 --> 01:19:47.463
I have listened to you very carefully,

826
01:19:47.563 --> 01:19:50.341
and I'm afraid it's not good news.

827
01:19:50.441 --> 01:19:52.982
You're a homosexual.

828
01:19:54.362 --> 01:19:58.283
Well, I don't really know
what kind of help I need, but I...

829
01:19:58.950 --> 01:20:02.395
I can't go on living
without knowing who I am.

830
01:20:02.495 --> 01:20:04.246
Please excuse me for a moment.

831
01:20:59.761 --> 01:21:02.352
Do you think I'm insane?

832
01:21:07.018 --> 01:21:08.795
Did a doctor say that?

833
01:21:08.895 --> 01:21:12.406
I'm sorry.
I know we agreed no more, but...

834
01:21:14.317 --> 01:21:15.343
Look at me.

835
01:21:15.443 --> 01:21:18.194
You are not insane.

836
01:21:22.700 --> 01:21:24.701
Did I do this to you?

837
01:21:25.620 --> 01:21:27.541
What?

838
01:21:30.833 --> 01:21:34.362
Sometimes, I... I wonder...

839
01:21:34.462 --> 01:21:36.072
If it hadn't been for the paintings...

840
01:21:36.172 --> 01:21:38.593
No. Gerda, no.

841
01:21:39.801 --> 01:21:44.432
You helped bring Lili to life,
but she was always there.

842
01:21:45.139 --> 01:21:46.541
She was always waiting.

843
01:21:46.641 --> 01:21:49.142
Now she's making you ill.

844
01:21:50.520 --> 01:21:52.901
I don't know what to do.

845
01:21:56.484 --> 01:21:59.245
The doctors can't help me.

846
01:22:03.992 --> 01:22:06.583
Do you want to try one more?

847
01:22:16.379 --> 01:22:18.531
...Warnekros, Einar. My husband.

848
01:22:18.631 --> 01:22:21.012
- Hello.
- Good to see you.

849
01:22:21.509 --> 01:22:23.119
So, what do you think would explain

850
01:22:23.219 --> 01:22:25.914
what you've been experiencing,
Mr. Wegener?

851
01:22:26.014 --> 01:22:28.935
Professor Warnekros, the fact is

852
01:22:31.269 --> 01:22:33.850
I believe that I am a woman,

853
01:22:35.189 --> 01:22:37.110
inside.

854
01:22:38.359 --> 01:22:40.780
And I believe it too.

855
01:22:47.327 --> 01:22:50.448
You probably think that I'm insane.

856
01:22:50.872 --> 01:22:53.441
Or that we both are.

857
01:22:53.541 --> 01:22:55.026
Well,

858
01:22:55.126 --> 01:22:58.547
there are people
who think that I'm insane.

859
01:23:02.175 --> 01:23:04.846
But I think you're probably right.

860
01:23:08.973 --> 01:23:12.644
I've met another man like you.

861
01:23:13.561 --> 01:23:15.797
I pursued his case,

862
01:23:15.897 --> 01:23:18.478
against the wishes of my colleagues,
of course.

863
01:23:19.233 --> 01:23:21.574
I told him I could operate

864
01:23:22.153 --> 01:23:24.454
to make him fully a woman.

865
01:23:25.698 --> 01:23:27.267
That was what he wanted.

866
01:23:27.367 --> 01:23:28.726
Is that really possible?

867
01:23:28.826 --> 01:23:30.395
What happened to the man?

868
01:23:30.495 --> 01:23:31.938
Was the operation successful?

869
01:23:32.038 --> 01:23:35.233
On the morning of the first operation,
he ran away.

870
01:23:35.333 --> 01:23:36.317
He was too frightened.

871
01:23:36.417 --> 01:23:39.153
I wouldn't do that. I...

872
01:23:39.253 --> 01:23:41.281
Perhaps he was the smart one.

873
01:23:41.381 --> 01:23:43.658
The surgery has never
been attempted before.

874
01:23:43.758 --> 01:23:45.839
Never.

875
01:23:47.261 --> 01:23:50.415
Professor Warnekros, what is the surgery?

876
01:23:50.515 --> 01:23:52.584
Two operations.

877
01:23:52.684 --> 01:23:55.355
The first, to remove
the male parts entirely.

878
01:23:56.521 --> 01:23:58.902
The second,
once you're strong enough again,

879
01:23:59.524 --> 01:24:01.525
to construct a vagina.

880
01:24:09.033 --> 01:24:11.374
An irreversible change

881
01:24:12.954 --> 01:24:15.375
and a high risk of failure.

882
01:24:15.790 --> 01:24:18.526
Infections. Complications.

883
01:24:18.626 --> 01:24:20.194
It's too dangerous.

884
01:24:20.294 --> 01:24:22.755
It's my only hope.

885
01:24:25.133 --> 01:24:27.974
I leave for Dresden at lunchtime tomorrow.

886
01:24:31.097 --> 01:24:33.468
Mrs. Wegener,

887
01:24:34.308 --> 01:24:37.139
I do believe I can help your husband.

888
01:24:38.312 --> 01:24:41.943
But he won't be your husband
when I've finished.

889
01:24:57.582 --> 01:24:59.359
I feel strange going dressed like this.

890
01:24:59.459 --> 01:25:01.420
It's important.

891
01:25:01.919 --> 01:25:03.905
Hans said
the Germans might check your papers.

892
01:25:04.005 --> 01:25:06.016
You're nearly there.

893
01:25:06.841 --> 01:25:09.092
I won't be seeing you again.

894
01:25:11.179 --> 01:25:14.600
I've only really liked
a handful of people in my life,

895
01:25:15.683 --> 01:25:17.601
and you've been two of them.

896
01:25:21.814 --> 01:25:23.825
Take care.

897
01:25:27.278 --> 01:25:29.199
Take care.

898
01:25:33.701 --> 01:25:36.542
I wish you'd let me come with you.

899
01:25:37.038 --> 01:25:38.959
I can't.

900
01:25:39.832 --> 01:25:42.293
You love Einar,

901
01:25:42.460 --> 01:25:44.751
and I have to let him go.

902
01:25:51.052 --> 01:25:52.893
Here.

903
01:25:53.262 --> 01:25:55.353
Take this.

904
01:27:51.005 --> 01:27:52.532
Hello.

905
01:27:52.632 --> 01:27:56.369
Um... My name is Lili.
I'm here to see Professor Warnekros.

906
01:27:56.469 --> 01:27:58.510
Lili what?

907
01:28:00.098 --> 01:28:01.874
Elbe.

908
01:28:01.974 --> 01:28:04.335
Lili Elbe, like the river.

909
01:28:04.435 --> 01:28:08.606
Of course. Please take a seat over there.

910
01:28:35.967 --> 01:28:38.128
Must I really wait?

911
01:28:38.302 --> 01:28:40.053
It's only a week.

912
01:28:40.888 --> 01:28:43.583
I need you to rest. Gain some weight.

913
01:28:43.683 --> 01:28:46.064
We can't risk an infection.

914
01:28:49.522 --> 01:28:52.273
For what we are attempting,

915
01:28:53.192 --> 01:28:55.863
I'll need you to be strong.

916
01:28:57.405 --> 01:28:59.746
This is not my body, Professor.

917
01:29:01.284 --> 01:29:03.795
Please take it away.

918
01:29:10.752 --> 01:29:13.093
You're having a baby.

919
01:29:14.756 --> 01:29:16.491
And you?

920
01:29:16.591 --> 01:29:19.342
Oh, no, no. I'm...

921
01:29:19.635 --> 01:29:21.454
I'm ill inside.

922
01:29:21.554 --> 01:29:23.998
But Professor Warnekros
is going to make me better.

923
01:29:24.098 --> 01:29:27.019
And will you be able
to have children after?

924
01:29:28.061 --> 01:29:30.442
Do you know, I don't know.

925
01:29:33.107 --> 01:29:35.358
I hope so.

926
01:29:39.656 --> 01:29:42.067
Gerda, why don't you go?

927
01:29:44.285 --> 01:29:46.479
- He asked me not to.
- He wanted to protect you.

928
01:29:46.579 --> 01:29:48.481
You should be there. I'll go with you.

929
01:29:48.581 --> 01:29:51.372
If I go, it will be alone.

930
01:29:52.710 --> 01:29:54.737
Now you're sounding like Einar.

931
01:29:54.837 --> 01:29:57.208
I am like Einar.

932
01:29:59.342 --> 01:30:01.202
What do you want me to do?

933
01:30:01.302 --> 01:30:03.162
I want you to go away.

934
01:30:03.262 --> 01:30:05.013
Really?

935
01:30:12.397 --> 01:30:15.318
No, I... Sorry.

936
01:31:20.548 --> 01:31:23.368
She regained consciousness very briefly.

937
01:31:23.468 --> 01:31:26.204
We're having to give her
a great deal of morphine, of course,

938
01:31:26.304 --> 01:31:28.206
so that's to be expected.

939
01:31:32.143 --> 01:31:33.878
You mustn't move, Lili.

940
01:31:33.978 --> 01:31:35.964
It only makes it worse.

941
01:31:36.064 --> 01:31:37.945
Oh, God.

942
01:31:38.274 --> 01:31:40.115
Breathe.

943
01:31:40.443 --> 01:31:41.761
Breathe.

944
01:31:41.861 --> 01:31:43.652
Breathe.

945
01:31:49.786 --> 01:31:51.947
I'm here.

946
01:31:59.837 --> 01:32:01.628
It's all right.

947
01:32:01.798 --> 01:32:03.969
I'm here now.

948
01:32:07.762 --> 01:32:10.013
Lili.

949
01:32:30.493 --> 01:32:34.544
I can feel myself getting better
when I listen to your pencil.

950
01:32:40.378 --> 01:32:42.839
You've always sketched me
better than I was.

951
01:32:45.383 --> 01:32:48.094
But what you draw, I become.

952
01:32:50.805 --> 01:32:53.186
You made me beautiful.

953
01:32:54.642 --> 01:32:57.353
And now you're making me strong.

954
01:33:00.648 --> 01:33:03.319
Such power in you.

955
01:33:09.574 --> 01:33:12.585
Shall we go back to Denmark, then, Gerda?

956
01:33:13.870 --> 01:33:16.751
Shall we go home?

957
01:33:34.182 --> 01:33:35.833
Lili!

958
01:33:35.933 --> 01:33:37.684
You're late.

959
01:33:40.104 --> 01:33:42.131
And your pills.

960
01:33:42.231 --> 01:33:45.301
Every two hours,
and I need to eat something first.

961
01:33:45.401 --> 01:33:48.242
I have some macaroons in my bag all ready.

962
01:33:49.113 --> 01:33:50.914
And these.

963
01:33:51.991 --> 01:33:53.952
Only if you need them.

964
01:34:01.751 --> 01:34:03.542
Good luck.

965
01:34:12.053 --> 01:34:16.791
And remember, making a purchase
at Fonnesbech's is not merely shopping.

966
01:34:16.891 --> 01:34:18.835
It's an experience.

967
01:34:18.935 --> 01:34:21.236
You lived in Paris, yes?

968
01:34:21.562 --> 01:34:22.547
Yes.

969
01:34:22.647 --> 01:34:25.800
Let everyone know. The store is a stage.

970
01:34:25.900 --> 01:34:29.151
We're here to perform.

971
01:34:34.575 --> 01:34:39.522
In Paris, you see, a lady would never dream
of spraying the scent directly onto herself.

972
01:34:39.622 --> 01:34:42.817
She... She would spray it in the air,

973
01:34:42.917 --> 01:34:45.069
and then she'd walk through it.

974
01:34:45.169 --> 01:34:47.210
- Oh.
- Voila.

975
01:34:48.297 --> 01:34:50.168
You try.

976
01:34:53.886 --> 01:34:56.507
Ah. Voila.

977
01:35:06.816 --> 01:35:08.009
Thanks.

978
01:35:08.109 --> 01:35:09.427
That's so unfair.

979
01:35:09.527 --> 01:35:12.972
You've got the sweetest tooth
and the narrowest hips in the whole store.

980
01:35:13.072 --> 01:35:15.183
How do you manage it,
eating so much sugar?

981
01:35:15.283 --> 01:35:17.268
The trick is you eat nothing else.

982
01:35:17.368 --> 01:35:19.659
- See you tomorrow.
- See you tomorrow.

983
01:35:21.539 --> 01:35:23.710
- Bye, Lili.
- Bye.

984
01:35:24.500 --> 01:35:26.671
Lili, are you coming?

985
01:35:32.175 --> 01:35:36.606
You know, one night last week,
I had the strangest dream.

986
01:35:37.096 --> 01:35:38.164
What was it?

987
01:35:38.264 --> 01:35:39.958
I dreamed you were getting married.

988
01:35:46.272 --> 01:35:48.049
Do you think I ever will?

989
01:35:48.149 --> 01:35:49.592
Who knows?

990
01:35:49.692 --> 01:35:53.113
So many strange things have happened.

991
01:35:53.821 --> 01:35:56.622
I do want to, Gerda.

992
01:35:58.034 --> 01:36:02.205
It's not so long ago we were married,
you and me.

993
01:36:04.457 --> 01:36:06.748
You and Einar.

994
01:36:09.587 --> 01:36:11.072
I know it was Einar.

995
01:36:11.172 --> 01:36:13.383
But really,

996
01:36:14.592 --> 01:36:18.093
it was you and me.

997
01:36:39.033 --> 01:36:41.124
Lili.

998
01:36:43.371 --> 01:36:45.212
Is it really you?

999
01:36:46.332 --> 01:36:48.383
I believe so.

1000
01:36:52.672 --> 01:36:56.263
So, what you're suggesting

1001
01:36:57.635 --> 01:37:00.216
is that, uh, a doctor

1002
01:37:02.056 --> 01:37:03.333
intervened.

1003
01:37:03.433 --> 01:37:06.252
To correct a mistake in nature.

1004
01:37:06.352 --> 01:37:08.254
He made you a woman.

1005
01:37:08.354 --> 01:37:10.506
No, God made me a woman.

1006
01:37:10.606 --> 01:37:12.926
But the doctor... He... The doctor

1007
01:37:13.026 --> 01:37:17.397
is curing me of the sickness
that was my disguise.

1008
01:37:20.575 --> 01:37:22.416
A real woman.

1009
01:37:40.011 --> 01:37:42.330
You're going to need a new notebook
if you carry on like that.

1010
01:37:42.430 --> 01:37:45.124
When Warnekros suggested I keep a diary,

1011
01:37:45.224 --> 01:37:48.185
I thought I'd never have
anything to write.

1012
01:37:49.062 --> 01:37:51.005
It does help,

1013
01:37:51.105 --> 01:37:52.840
just to make sense of things.

1014
01:37:52.940 --> 01:37:55.134
Maybe I should try it.

1015
01:38:00.156 --> 01:38:01.947
So,

1016
01:38:02.617 --> 01:38:05.061
do you enjoy working at Fonnesbech's?

1017
01:38:05.161 --> 01:38:06.896
For now, at least.

1018
01:38:06.996 --> 01:38:09.691
I do enjoy sort of being part of it.

1019
01:38:09.791 --> 01:38:12.082
You never think of painting?

1020
01:38:14.754 --> 01:38:15.780
You might be good at it.

1021
01:38:15.880 --> 01:38:19.131
Gerda, I want to be a woman,
not a painter.

1022
01:38:19.509 --> 01:38:22.550
Well, people have been known to do both.

1023
01:38:26.265 --> 01:38:29.085
I'm curious to see what you would paint.

1024
01:38:29.185 --> 01:38:31.546
That's all. Sometimes it's hard
to know what's in your...

1025
01:38:31.646 --> 01:38:34.340
Didn't you just take one of those
a minute ago?

1026
01:38:34.440 --> 01:38:36.821
Gerda, I know what I'm doing.

1027
01:38:40.154 --> 01:38:42.785
I'm just going to get some fresh air.

1028
01:38:43.658 --> 01:38:46.102
You know, sometimes I do wonder
why you let me go through all this,

1029
01:38:46.202 --> 01:38:48.229
if you thought that
everything would be the same afterwards.

1030
01:38:48.329 --> 01:38:50.580
I didn't.

1031
01:38:50.707 --> 01:38:52.692
But I promised Einar
that I would take care of you.

1032
01:38:52.792 --> 01:38:55.069
For goodness' sakes, Gerda, Einar is dead.

1033
01:38:55.169 --> 01:38:57.590
We both have to accept that.

1034
01:38:58.923 --> 01:39:01.451
You took care of me,
but now I have to take care of myself.

1035
01:39:01.551 --> 01:39:04.392
I have to have a life of my own.

1036
01:39:05.513 --> 01:39:08.314
And you need to do the same.

1037
01:39:10.893 --> 01:39:12.774
Come on, Hvap.

1038
01:39:28.411 --> 01:39:29.980
Uh, yes.

1039
01:39:30.663 --> 01:39:32.584
In London.

1040
01:39:33.333 --> 01:39:34.859
Uh, is it urgent?

1041
01:39:34.959 --> 01:39:37.130
No, that's fine.

1042
01:39:37.337 --> 01:39:39.338
Just tell him...

1043
01:39:40.923 --> 01:39:43.724
Just say it's a beautiful day
in Copenhagen.

1044
01:39:48.890 --> 01:39:51.641
- Morning.
- Good morning.

1045
01:40:14.916 --> 01:40:17.860
It's not what you think.
Henrik's homosexual.

1046
01:40:17.960 --> 01:40:20.671
There's nothing between us.

1047
01:40:21.673 --> 01:40:23.866
I should have told you that I'd seen him.

1048
01:40:23.966 --> 01:40:25.994
No, you shouldn't.

1049
01:40:26.094 --> 01:40:28.204
He's a friend, Gerdie, someone to talk to.

1050
01:40:28.304 --> 01:40:31.065
Because you can't talk to me.

1051
01:40:31.933 --> 01:40:34.524
I've made a decision.

1052
01:40:35.103 --> 01:40:37.839
I'm going back to Dresden
for the second operation.

1053
01:40:37.939 --> 01:40:39.132
That's too soon.

1054
01:40:39.232 --> 01:40:40.925
No... No, it's time.

1055
01:40:41.025 --> 01:40:43.094
I need to finish what I started.

1056
01:40:43.194 --> 01:40:47.159
- You're not strong enough.
- Professor Warnekros thinks that I am.

1057
01:40:47.281 --> 01:40:50.268
Warnekros? Warnekros hasn't seen you.

1058
01:40:50.368 --> 01:40:52.329
I've made up my mind, Gerda.

1059
01:40:52.787 --> 01:40:54.063
It could kill you.

1060
01:40:54.163 --> 01:40:57.084
I'm going on Friday.
Will you come with me?

1061
01:41:00.461 --> 01:41:03.552
I won't help you to hurt yourself.

1062
01:41:20.314 --> 01:41:22.575
Gerda, will you come?

1063
01:41:43.629 --> 01:41:46.760
This will be harder
than the first operation.

1064
01:41:47.425 --> 01:41:49.386
You understand that?

1065
01:41:49.844 --> 01:41:53.055
Yes, I do.

1066
01:41:54.807 --> 01:41:57.428
It's complex surgery.

1067
01:41:58.853 --> 01:42:02.564
And I will sleep all the way through it.

1068
01:42:05.151 --> 01:42:06.261
Yes, you will.

1069
01:42:06.361 --> 01:42:09.572
And you'll be there when I wake up.

1070
01:42:11.157 --> 01:42:13.278
Of course.

1071
01:42:13.534 --> 01:42:16.705
I want a husband who looks just like you.

1072
01:42:19.332 --> 01:42:20.942
Um...

1073
01:42:21.042 --> 01:42:23.793
Maybe a child one day.

1074
01:42:27.298 --> 01:42:29.799
Like a real woman.

1075
01:42:30.468 --> 01:42:33.049
One step at a time.

1076
01:42:39.852 --> 01:42:42.693
Get some rest. Good night.

1077
01:42:54.617 --> 01:42:56.908
Are you still angry with me?

1078
01:42:57.578 --> 01:43:00.079
I'm not angry with you.

1079
01:43:01.290 --> 01:43:03.881
I'm worried about you.

1080
01:43:04.919 --> 01:43:07.710
You heard my wish, Gerda.

1081
01:43:08.548 --> 01:43:11.129
When no one else could hear me,

1082
01:43:11.676 --> 01:43:14.007
you did.

1083
01:43:18.182 --> 01:43:20.043
Come.

1084
01:43:20.143 --> 01:43:22.503
We both need our rest.

1085
01:43:22.603 --> 01:43:24.524
I'll sleep on the chair there.

1086
01:43:25.857 --> 01:43:28.468
- No, off to your little hotel.
- I don't mind.

1087
01:43:28.568 --> 01:43:30.053
Here, take this.

1088
01:43:30.153 --> 01:43:32.404
Because there's a chill in the air.

1089
01:43:34.449 --> 01:43:36.643
- No.
- Please.

1090
01:43:36.743 --> 01:43:39.794
You have it. For now.

1091
01:43:40.747 --> 01:43:43.208
I'm going to be fine.

1092
01:43:43.499 --> 01:43:45.380
Yes.

1093
01:43:56.179 --> 01:43:58.039
Sleep well.

1094
01:43:58.139 --> 01:44:00.310
Good night.

1095
01:44:47.814 --> 01:44:49.707
Good evening.

1096
01:44:51.192 --> 01:44:52.677
Uh, room nine, please.

1097
01:44:52.777 --> 01:44:55.941
- Number nine, yes, of course.
- Thank you.

1098
01:45:01.869 --> 01:45:03.950
Hans.

1099
01:45:14.173 --> 01:45:15.825
It's all right.

1100
01:45:15.925 --> 01:45:19.176
Everything will be all right.

1101
01:45:36.779 --> 01:45:38.990
Miss Elbe.

1102
01:45:40.241 --> 01:45:42.202
It's time.

1103
01:45:54.339 --> 01:45:57.090
Good luck, everybody.

1104
01:46:03.890 --> 01:46:06.141
Swab, quick.

1105
01:46:15.443 --> 01:46:18.704
Professor Warnekros would like a word.

1106
01:46:21.074 --> 01:46:22.934
She lost a lot of blood.

1107
01:46:23.034 --> 01:46:25.687
Now we are struggling
to keep the fever down.

1108
01:46:25.787 --> 01:46:29.038
There's a chance it might
burn itself out, but...

1109
01:46:32.669 --> 01:46:34.790
I have to be honest.

1110
01:46:35.630 --> 01:46:37.801
The prognosis is not...

1111
01:46:41.678 --> 01:46:44.849
Come here. Just lie still.

1112
01:46:45.431 --> 01:46:48.222
It's all right. Shh.

1113
01:46:59.237 --> 01:47:01.398
Shh.

1114
01:47:32.603 --> 01:47:34.654
Lili.

1115
01:47:50.455 --> 01:47:52.296
How are you, Lili?

1116
01:48:01.257 --> 01:48:03.428
I am

1117
01:48:03.760 --> 01:48:07.551
entirely myself.

1118
01:48:10.183 --> 01:48:13.024
You had us worried there, you know?

1119
01:48:15.063 --> 01:48:18.984
Can we go outside, Gerda?

1120
01:48:21.277 --> 01:48:23.179
Into the garden?

1121
01:48:23.279 --> 01:48:25.660
You should rest.

1122
01:48:30.995 --> 01:48:33.036
Please.

1123
01:48:52.767 --> 01:48:56.648
You mustn't worry about me anymore, Gerda.

1124
01:48:58.231 --> 01:49:00.612
It's an old habit.

1125
01:49:01.359 --> 01:49:03.150
I'm slow to change.

1126
01:49:08.408 --> 01:49:12.539
How have I ever deserved such love?

1127
01:49:18.167 --> 01:49:21.798
There's nothing to be afraid of anymore.

1128
01:49:22.505 --> 01:49:24.546
No.

1129
01:49:27.301 --> 01:49:29.472
Last night

1130
01:49:30.722 --> 01:49:34.393
I had the most beautiful dream.

1131
01:49:37.520 --> 01:49:43.191
I dreamed that I was a baby
in my mother's arms.

1132
01:49:45.945 --> 01:49:48.696
And she looked down at me,

1133
01:49:51.200 --> 01:49:54.201
and she called me Lili.

1134
01:49:56.205 --> 01:49:58.496
Lili.

1135
01:50:24.108 --> 01:50:25.979
Lili?

1136
01:50:34.535 --> 01:50:36.826
Lili!

1137
01:51:50.820 --> 01:51:53.031
No, leave it!

1138
01:51:58.536 --> 01:52:00.867
Let it fly.
